-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for Magna Carta (1215), McKechnie translation.
-- Every expected value below was decided in ANSWERS.md (written before any .l4 file in this directory was opened),
-- and is written here from that file, never from the encoding's output.  Each comment gives the scenario number
-- (S<n>, as numbered in ANSWERS.md) and the provision.  An assertion that failed was a finding and was left failing.
-- Of the 488 assertions, 34 failed on the first run against the final modules of the encoder's first round; the encoder then repaired six
-- of them and, in a second round, moved 17 more branches to the text's no. On 2026-10-30 the lead restated 38 assertions (28 after the first run,
-- 10 after the second round), each with a -- RECONCILED comment that quotes the original.
-- Convention used to put my answers in the encoding's vocabulary: "lawful? NO" / "forbidden? YES" = Barred;
-- "lawful? YES" / "forbidden? NO" = `Not barred`; NC = the encoding's own "... not covered" constructor.
-- Money: ANSWERS.md says 100 pounds (= 2000s, 20s to the pound).  The encoding keeps pounds and shillings apart on
-- purpose (nouns module), so the sums are asserted in the unit the text uses (Pounds 100, Shillings 100); that is a
-- difference of representation, not of answer.
-- Scenarios the encoding has no function for are not asserted here; they are the -- GAP lines at the end of this file.

§ `Independent tests, by chapter`

§§ `Chapter 1`
#ASSERT `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled -- S14 [1.5] liberties held by the heirs of freemen
#ASSERT `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Entitled -- S14 [1.5] a freeman is a grantee (seat question Q1 also)
#ASSERT `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered` -- S16 [1.5] a villein (neither freeman nor heir of one) is not named

§§ `Chapters 2 and 3`
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the sum the Charter names for a whole holding of this kind` `a whole earl's barony` EQUALS (Pounds 100) -- S18 [2.2] earl's barony 100 pounds (= 2000s)
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole earl's barony` (JUST 101) EQUALS (JUST (Pounds 100)) -- S19 [2.2] 101 pounds is not chargeable on an earl's heir
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the sum the Charter names for a whole holding of this kind` `a whole barony` EQUALS (Pounds 100) -- S20 [2.3] baron's barony 100 pounds
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole barony` NOTHING EQUALS (JUST (Pounds 100)) -- S21 [2.3] 100 pounds is chargeable on a baron's heir
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the sum the Charter names for a whole holding of this kind` `a whole knight's fee` EQUALS (Shillings 100) -- S22 [2.4] knight's fee: 100s at most
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the knight's relief, which is 100s at most` (JUST 100) EQUALS (JUST (Shillings 100)) -- S23 [2.4] 100s is chargeable on a knight's fee
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the knight's relief, which is 100s at most` (JUST 101) EQUALS (JUST (Shillings 100)) -- S24 [2.4] 101s is not chargeable (capped at 100s)
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the knight's relief, which is 100s at most` (JUST 60) EQUALS (JUST (Shillings 60)) -- S25 [2.4-2.5] 60s is chargeable
