§§ `Chapter 4`
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred` -- S36 [4.1] reasonable produce, no waste
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred -- S37 [4.1] more than reasonable produce
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred -- S38 [4.1] destruction or waste
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the consequence for a guardian of this kind who has made waste` `committed by the King to the sheriff or another accountable to him` EQUALS `The King takes amends and the land is committed to two lawful and discreet men of that fee` -- S39,S40,S41 [4.2-4.3] sheriff or accountable keeper: amends, and two men
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the consequence for a guardian of this kind who has made waste` `given or sold by the King to someone` EQUALS `The wardship is lost and transferred to two lawful and discreet men of that fief` -- S42,S43 [4.4] given or sold: wardship lost, two men
#ASSERT NOT (`ch 4 -- the consequence for a guardian of this kind who has made waste` `given or sold by the King to someone` EQUALS `The King takes amends and the land is committed to two lawful and discreet men of that fee`) -- S44 [4.4] no amends are stated for a grantee (indirect check)
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- what follows if the guardian lays waste` `given or sold by the King to someone` FALSE EQUALS `Nothing follows under chapter 4` -- S45 [4] no waste: nothing follows (NC)
#ASSERT `ch 5 -- the restoration is what the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE -- S51 [5.2] all land restored, stocked as the season and issues require
#ASSERT `ch 5 -- the restoration is what the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE -- S52 [5.2] stocking beyond what the issues can reasonably bear is not required

